# rex-parity — Rex 0.3: site and app parity. Rex keeps what makes it unique (five
# declarations, one page folder, one checker, one DOM, nine states, a text renderer, Hono
# plus oRPC, no RSC) and adopts, the Rex way, what Astro gives sites and Next.js gives apps.
# Format: sectioned KV (.kvx); strings double-quoted.

[meta]
feature    = "rex-parity"
name       = "Rex 0.3: site and app parity"
slug       = "rex-parity"
version    = "0.3.0"
status     = "in_progress"
intro      = "Rex 0.2 is a production standard and the Rex site proved it with a static deployment. Building that site and auditing Rex against Astro (sites) and Next.js (web applications) exposed what a user of either expects and Rex lacks: a declared document head, content collections, islands, declared redirects, host adapters, a typed env, section frames, a Link, prefetch, CDN caching, on-demand regeneration, HTTP endpoints for read actions, a site starter, generators and a developer loop with findings in the browser. 0.3 adopts each as one declared, derived, addressed and checked pattern, never a second pattern for a problem Rex already solves, and never a wheel reinvented where a proven shape exists."
goal       = "Ship @sidioralabs/rex 0.3.0 where every P0 and P1 gap of the parity audits is closed by a declaration or a derived surface that the manifest, the sidecar, the text renderer and rex check all know, with the demo using every adopted feature and rex new --template site producing a Rex site like site/ that builds, checks and walks clean."
scope      = "Declaration groundwork (page, action, config, manifest, sidecar, errors), document head and SEO, navigation and failure boundaries, caching and targets, content collections and markdown, host adapters and preview, islands, i18n for static sites, the developer loop and the shipped walk, images and fonts, the routing contract (rest segments, not-found, redirects, statuses), mutations driving caches, env and the server entry, derived endpoints, the derived shell, generators and hygiene, the demo and the site template."
completion = "Every task done with its verify_cmd evidence; rex check reports zero findings on the demo, the site and both rex new templates; the demo operability walk, no-JS walk, axe, vitals and Lighthouse (performance, accessibility, best practices and SEO) pass through the shipped walk helpers; rex build on node, edge and static targets writes the derived files the audits name; docs and recipes describe each feature in the task that ships it."

[decision]
groundwork          = "0.3 adds fields to the five declarations and to rex.config, never a sixth declaration and never a file convention: chrome gains description, image, frame, order and icon; page gains islands, prefetch, fallback and a paths form { action, map }; routes gain a rest segment; action gains http, cache and optimistic; ActionContext gains env, locale and density; rex.config gains site, redirects, deploy, env, prefetch, security.forwarded, images.remote, fonts[].variable and fallback, i18n.direction. Every field is validated at declaration with a REX code, written into the manifest, AGENTS.md and the sidecar where it describes the page an agent operates, and readable statically by rex check. One wave-0 task owns these files so every later task consumes a declared field and never edits core/page.ts, core/action.ts, core/config.ts or manifest/*."
metadata            = "The document head is declared on the page and in rex.config, never in a component and never by a function that fetches: rex.config site { origin, name, description, image, titleTemplate } and page chrome { title, description, image } where title and description accept a literal, a msg: key or {param} placeholders filled from the validated route params by the message formatter, so one page declaration titles every prerendered path. documentHead derives title, description, canonical, Open Graph, twitter:card, robots, hreflang alternates and a rel=alternate link to the markdown rendering; the h1, the announcer, the palette, the text renderer, the manifest and the sidecar document field carry the same resolved values; the non-script head of index.html reaches every document in dev and production and Rex removes from it the tags it owns. No generateMetadata, no metadata export, no head component."
layouts             = "Nested layouts are section frames, one level by design: chrome.frame names an export of the frames map in the ui.components module (page.ts stays React-free), ShellFrame renders it with data-rex-frame and the derived section links of the pages sharing the frame, keyed by name so it persists across navigations inside the section; chrome.order and chrome.icon order and decorate the derived navigation; the breadcrumb trail derives from chrome.back. No layout.tsx, template.tsx, route groups, parallel or intercepting routes, no per-page component overrides."
islands             = "The island is the region, the unit that already carries an address, an error boundary and a sidecar entry. page.islands maps a declared region to load, idle, visible or never: a static page hydrates only the regions it lists, each as its own chunk measured under the page budget, booted by a nonce'd script at the declared moment; an ssr, ssg or csr page defaults every region to load and may defer one to idle or visible or leave it server-only with never. An unhydrated region's actions work as forms; addresses, the sidecar and the nine states do not change. No component-site client:* directives, no client:only, no second renderer."
content_collections = "A collection is an entity, a store and two read actions, never a sixth declaration: contentStore(entity, { dir, pattern }) and fileStore(entity, file) implement Store<T> over app/content/<name> with frontmatter validated by the entity and the body held by the markdown() field kind, which the store renders once per file through renderMarkdown; a page reaches the collection through a read action listed in load, and paths: { action, map } runs that action through the router as the build actor so page.ts never calls a handler. Prose and Toc are the one way rendered markdown reaches the DOM (through unsafeHtml with data-rex-prose) and the text renderer serves the markdown source. No MDX, no content.config.ts, no import.meta.glob of content from components."
images              = "Img stays the one image primitive and images in rex.config the one config block, made live at build: a Vite hook writes the images.sizes by images.formats variants of every local Img source through sharp (optional peer), Img fills srcset from them when sizes is set and renders one picture element per extra format, width and height stay required, remote sources must match images.remote. Fonts gain a CSS variable and a metric-matched fallback face computed from the font file, and reach client-rendered documents. No runtime optimizer route, no loader abstraction, no Picture component, no blur placeholders, no CDN fonts."
redirects           = "Redirects are declared once in rex.config redirects (source route syntax including params and the rest segment, destination route or absolute URL, status 301, 302, 307 or 308, default 308) and derived into a server route before the render route, the client router's resolution of an unmatched path, the manifest and AGENTS.md, a meta-refresh stub with a canonical link and a visible data-rex-nav link on the static target, and the host writers' native files. No imperative redirect() from render code, no rewrites, no URL masking."
adapters            = "rex build --target stays the one runtime switch and deploy.host in rex.config the one host switch: each host maps to exactly one target and one writer in cli/hosts/<host>.ts that emits the host's files over the unchanged fetch-only server (wrangler.jsonc, .vercel/output, netlify.toml, deno.json, Dockerfile and .dockerignore, .nojekyll), so prerendered HTML, index.md, rex/manifest and 404.html are the same files on every host; the edge target prerenders and serves revalidate pages through a Cache-API store; Cache-Control derives from render, revalidate and the actor; rex preview serves any build. No per-route runtime, no base path, no host APIs in app code."
env                 = "Environment is a schema in rex.config env { client, server } written with the rex/schema field helpers: client keys start with VITE_ and are inlined at build, server keys are the secrets, read on node, bun and deno from process.env and on edge from the bindings the adapter receives, validated once at start (REX451) and reachable only as ctx.env in handlers or import { env } from rex:env in app/server modules; secretNames derives from the server keys and .env.example from the schema. No dotenv dependency, no process.env in app code, no host bindings outside the adapter."
templates           = "rex new --template app|site selects a generator set in the one generator chain; both templates are ordinary Rex apps on the five declarations, the page folder convention and the DesignX standard, gated by rex check and a built-in page test. The site template is a Rex site like site/: static render default, a content collection, a Prose page and the derived head, sitemap and feed files. --example fetches a folder of the repository examples; --host fills deploy.host. No layout, linter, language or bundler options."
navigation          = "One way to navigate: Link in markup (parts, overlays, states, app/components) and nav.to in regions, both through pageHref and the same route change, both addressed by data-rex-nav, both typed by the page declaration or the generated page id union; the back and recovery controls are Links so static pages work without JavaScript; a push scrolls to the top or the hash and a traverse restores; prefetch is declared on the page (page.prefetch, config default) and never as a per-anchor prop; under REX_STATIC_HOST every Link navigates by document."
caching             = "One vocabulary drives every cache: a read action may declare cache { maxAge, scope } for the server, a mutating action's invalidates names loaders and read actions, and from those names Rex derives the client refetch, the server cache purge, the background regeneration of every prerendered page whose loaders the action invalidates, and the optimistic value a region shows while the mutation is pending (action.optimistic, a subset of invalidates). No use cache, cacheLife, cacheTag, revalidatePath or revalidateTag."
endpoints           = "A read action exposed over HTTP is the same declaration with action.http { method, path, contentType, csrf }: the route inherits policy, validation, audit, the manifest row and AGENTS.md; GET endpoints whose input accepts {} are prerendered to files on every target that prerenders, so a static site ships sitemap.xml, feeds and a search index from declarations. sitemap.xml, robots.txt and llms.txt derive from the manifest and the prerender list when site.origin is set. No route.ts, no endpoint files, no hand-written Hono routes as the way to read data."
not_found           = "The 404 page is an ordinary page folder with the reserved id not-found (route /404, chrome.nav false): the router resolves an unmatched path to it, the server answers 404 with its HTML and markdown, the static target prerenders it as 404.html, and the built-in fallback stays for apps without it. HTTP statuses follow the state the page already shows: invalid route params and a loader 404 answer 404 with the TerminalError state, a loader 403 answers 403, everything else stays 500 with RecoverableError. No notFound() thrown from render code, no not-found.tsx per segment."
i18n_static         = "A prerendered app with several locales uses prefix routing: prerender writes one document, index.md and sidecar per locale, the static cache keys by path and locale, the server redirects an unprefixed document request and sets Content-Language and Vary, the root document of a static build is a locale chooser with addressed links, and locale is a first-class affordance (sidecar, manifest, AGENTS.md, a shell locale switcher with data-rex-locale, the reserved ?locale= key). Framework chrome strings are rex.* messages with shipped English defaults. No per-locale page folders, no locale middleware file, no runtime i18n library."
dev_loop            = "rex check stays the one checker and the browser shows its findings: rex() reads rex.config.ts wherever it runs (vitest included), a Vite hook re-runs the synchronous rules on change and sends findings to a devtools Check panel, runtime failures reach an Errors panel with code, hint and docs link, the devtools open by click, shortcut and URL, and the operability walk ships as @sidioralabs/rex/testing/playwright so every app runs the same gate the demo and the site run. No dev toolbar plugin API, no MCP server, no second rule engine."
not_adopted         = "Rex does not adopt: file-system-derived routes and bracketed folders (the route is declared in page.ts); React Server Components, use client and use server, Server Actions, server layouts and async server components; MDX or any component syntax inside content; per-segment loading, error, not-found and template files (states.tsx and the nine states own them); parallel and intercepting routes (regions and URL-bound overlays); component-site hydration directives (client:load, client:visible, client:only, next/dynamic at the import site); multi-framework islands and the .astro format; imperative redirect(), notFound(), Astro.redirect() or Astro.rewrite thrown from render code; rewrites and URL masking; a middleware or proxy file convention and a locals bag (the server factory, the actor resolver and the policy are the request hooks); route.ts and endpoint files; use cache, cacheLife, cacheTag, fetch-level caching and revalidateTag; route segment config exports (dynamic, revalidate, fetchCache, runtime, experimental_ppr); generateMetadata, metadata exports, next/head and freeform head components; transition:name, transition:animate and transition:persist attributes; next/script worker strategy and inline script children; an on-demand image optimizer route, pluggable image loaders and services, blur placeholders, fill layout and a Picture component; generated Open Graph images in the core; file-based metadata conventions (sitemap.ts, robots.ts, icon.png, opengraph-image, rss.xml.js); fonts from a CDN at runtime; a base path and locale domains; per-route runtime selection; host runtime APIs in app code; output file tracing; per-locale page folders and fallback page rewrites; a content.config.ts registry; Astro.glob and import.meta.glob of content; Server Actions as exported functions; arbitrary useQuery or custom Hono routes as the way to read data; a second config file, bundler flags, a lint wrapper, CLI telemetry, layout, linter, JavaScript or language starter options; a dev toolbar app API and an MCP server; vendor RUM destinations; toast-style progress bars; chrome.components per page."

[design]
module_layout       = "New modules, each registered in one list: server/: middleware/cache.ts and middleware/locale.ts (REX_MIDDLEWARE), routes/redirect.ts, routes/http.ts, routes/sitemap.ts, routes/locale.ts (REX_ROUTES), cache.ts (the action cache with memoryCache), adapters/static-host.ts (the static host semantics of tools/serve-static.mjs). vite/: outputs.ts (ordered StaticOutput writers run by build.ts after prerender) with outputs/<name>.ts per derived file (shell-documents, static-manifest, text-files, prerender-list, headers, redirects, sitemap, robots, llms, endpoints, not-found, locale-chooser), images.ts, fonts.ts, env-module.ts, check.ts, config-file.ts (REX_HOOKS). client/: link.tsx, prefetch.ts, islands.ts, content/ (prose.tsx, toc.tsx, index.ts, the rex/client/content entry), shell/document.tsx and shell/locale-slot.tsx (SHELL_SLOTS). store/: content.ts and markdown.ts behind the rex/store/content entry. check/rules/: document.ts, content.ts, deploy.ts, tests.ts (defaultRules). cli/: hosts/index.ts with hosts/<host>.ts, commands/preview.ts, upgrade.ts, add.ts, gen/site.ts, gen/example.ts, gen/test.ts, gen/repo.ts (REX_NEW_GENERATORS), versions.ts. testing/: playwright.ts (the rex/testing/playwright entry) and vitest.ts. src/errors.ts is the rex/errors entry."
shared_lists        = "Registration lists and export maps that any task may append one entry to without listing them in touches: vite/hooks.ts, vite/outputs.ts, server/routes.ts, server/middleware.ts, client/shell/slots.ts, client/providers.ts, check/rules/index.ts, cli/generators.ts, cli/hosts/index.ts, cli/index.ts (commands register by file), every index.ts under packages/rex/src, packages/rex/package.json, typedoc.json, tools/freshness.mjs, examples/demo/package.json, site/package.json, the root package.json and pnpm-lock.yaml. Hub docs are shared the same way, section-owned: docs/primitives.md, docs/cli.md, docs/platforms.md, docs/agent-contract.md, docs/convention.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/recipes/README.md, docs/errors.md (regenerated by tools/docs-errors.mjs), README.md; a task edits only the section, table rows or recipe link it names in its do_ lines. A recipe under docs/recipes/<name>.md is owned by one task and listed in its touches. Generated files examples/demo/.rex/manifest.json and examples/demo/AGENTS.md are regenerated with rex manifest by whoever changes the demo. The qualification log spec/rex-parity/qualification.kvx is shared and never in touches. Conflicts in shared files are resolved by the feature manager by union; in generated files by regenerating."
errors              = "New catalog codes, all in core/errors.ts with hints in core/errors.docs.ts: REX124 site config, REX125 env schema, REX126 redirects, REX127 deploy; REX225 chrome fields (description, image, frame, order, icon, placeholders naming an undeclared param), REX226 islands (a region not declared, a value outside load idle visible never, never on a region whose action has a shortcut), REX227 action.http (method, path under /rex, collision with a page route or another action, GET on a non-read action), REX228 action.cache (non-read action, maxAge not a positive whole number, scope outside shared actor locale), REX229 action.optimistic (a key outside invalidates, a key naming a non-read action), REX230 the reserved page id not-found (route must be /404 and chrome.nav false) and fallback without paths; REX335 page render failed (the page boundary); REX451 env invalid or missing at server start. Checker findings keep rule ids; the REX5xx entries for new rule families are added by the task that adds the rule."
declaration_surface = "core/page.ts: parseRoute accepts :name* as the last segment only (RouteSegment kind rest; the params schema must declare it as a required array of strings, or an array accepting [] for :name*?); PageChrome { header, nav, back, title, description?, image?, frame?, order?, icon? }; page options islands, prefetch (hover | viewport | none), fallback (render | not-found, only with paths), paths as () => params[] or { action: ReadAction, map: (output) => params[] }; the reserved id not-found; resolveChromeText(template, params) fills {param} placeholders without React. core/action.ts: http?: { method: GET | POST, path, contentType?, csrf? }, cache?: { maxAge, scope? }, optimistic?: Record<name, (current, input) => next>; ActionContext { actor, env, locale, density }. core/config.ts: site, redirects, deploy { host }, env { client, server }, prefetch, security.forwarded, images.remote, fonts[].variable and fallback, i18n.direction. core/protocol.ts: RESERVED_QUERY_KEYS gains locale and devtools. manifest/types.ts and build.ts: pages[].chrome (description, image, frame, order, icon), pages[].islands, prefetch, fallback, routeParams with rest, actions[].http, cache, optimistic, app.site, redirects, deploy, i18n; buildManifest validates action.invalidates names (loader name, read action id or page id), http path collisions and redirect sources against page routes. sidecar.schema.ts and client/agent/sidecar.tsx: document { title, description, canonical }, loaders [{ name, action, invalidatedBy, defer? }], locale and locales, direction, frame, and the region entry fields island and optimistic; pages-text.ts prints the Loaders table and the document rows. agents-md.ts lists redirects, deploy, endpoints, islands and locales."
head_pipeline       = "server/ssr.ts documentHead(assets, page, params, data, site, locale): charset, viewport, resolved title through site.titleTemplate, meta description, link canonical (site.origin plus the routed localized path), og:title, og:description, og:url, og:image, og:type, og:site_name, twitter:card, meta robots for noindex, link alternate hreflang per locale plus x-default under prefix routing, link alternate type text/markdown to the page's text rendering, font preloads, the font-face block with the family variable and the fallback face when the FontSpec carries metrics, image preloads, stylesheets, modulepreloads, then assets.head filtered of every owned tag; the same helper builds the form confirmation and error pages. For a static page the renderer emits no module script, no modulepreload and no rex+data script in every environment and runs the missing-forms check as REX405 at render in dev. vite/ssr-css.ts readSsrAssets reads the non-script head of dist/client/index.html; vite/ssr.ts transforms the app's own index.html in dev. client/shell/document.tsx updates document.title, canonical and description on route change from the sidecar document field."
navigation_runtime  = "client/link.tsx Link { page | id, params?, search?, replace?, scroll? } renders a[data-rex-nav] with the typed href, navigates through useRouteChange with the target's transition, prefetches per the target's declared strategy (client/prefetch.ts: pointerenter and focus, or one IntersectionObserver; backs off under saveData, 2g and agent density; a document prefetch link under REX_STATIC_HOST), and performs a document navigation under REX_STATIC_HOST. nav.to, nav.href and nav.replace accept a page declaration or a page id typed by the RexPageId union that the app module writes into rex:app typings. RexRoutes keeps a per-entry scroll position map with history.scrollRestoration manual. PageBoundary (client/boundary.tsx) wraps the page body, records REX335 to the outcome store, marks the reserved region id page in the failure registry and renders the page's RecoverableError with a remount retry; AppBoundary wraps the Shell with the startup error markup."
islands_runtime     = "vite/split.ts adds an island chunk group island-<page>-<region> measured under the page budget; vite/app-module.ts imports a listed region through its own loader; server/ssr.ts emits for a static page a modulepreload per island and one nonce'd boot script, and for hydrated pages a Suspense boundary whose lazy importer resolves at the declared moment; client/islands.ts hydrates a section with hydrateRoot through the provider stack of mountRexPage scoped to the page runtime, now for load, on requestIdleCallback for idle, on IntersectionObserver for visible, adopts the page's existing sidecar script and handles ?act= on boot; the section carries data-rex-island and data-rex-hydrated; check/rules/render.ts static-needs-js reports a non-island region of a static page that imports act, useAct, useOverlay, useLoader, useStore or a page hook, and region-needs-js reports a never region referencing an action with a shortcut; parity/runtime mounts islands."
content_pipeline    = "core/store.ts ListQuery gains sort { field, direction } and range filters lt, lte, gt, gte and in, validated by normalizeListQuery (REX329) and bind (REX305), implemented by memoryStore, drizzleStore and contentStore and proven by core/store.conformance.ts. schema/fields.ts gains markdown() (kind markdown, value { source, html, headings, text }). store/markdown.ts renderMarkdown(source, { slug, links }) on marked and shiki (optional peers, never in a client bundle) returns html with heading ids, headings and text. store/content.ts contentStore and fileStore read app/content, key by file slug, fill the markdown field at read time cached by file digest, and refuse put and delete with REX329. check/engine.ts gives app/content the content role (importable by no role); check/rules/content.ts reports invalid-entry (file and frontmatter line) and unbound (a collection folder no store binds); parity/paths-handler reports a paths that references .handler(. vite/prerender.ts expandPagePaths runs { action, map } through createActionLoaderRunner as the build actor. client/content/prose.tsx renders through unsafeHtml with data-rex-prose; toc.tsx renders headings as links. The text renderer appends the markdown source of a markdown field after the sidecar."
cache_pipeline      = "server/middleware/cache.ts derives Cache-Control after the route runs from x-rex-render, x-rex-static, the page's render and revalidate, and the actor: a prerendered page for the anonymous actor answers public, max-age=0, s-maxage=31536000, must-revalidate, or with revalidate n public, max-age=0, s-maxage=n, stale-while-revalidate=n; an actor render, ssr, csr, denied or failed answers private, no-store; Vary carries Cookie, x-rex-density and the Client Hint names; index.md follows its page; GET /rex/manifest answers an ETag and 304. adapters/node.ts serves /assets/ hashed files immutable. vite/outputs/headers.ts writes dist/client/_headers for static hosts and the host writers copy the table. The edge target runs prerenderBuild, imports dist/prerender.json at build time, and installEdgeStaticPages(registry, { list, store }) with cacheStaticStore over the Cache API and an after(promise) hook bound to executionCtx.waitUntil serves and regenerates like node. security.forwarded reads X-Forwarded-Proto and X-Forwarded-Host as the request origin in the Origin check, CORS and createRexContext."
invalidation        = "server/cache.ts memoryCache() (get, set, purge by action id and scope) and createRexServer cache?: Cache; actionProcedure in server/router.ts wraps a read action with cache after the policy check (key: action id, input digest, actor id or locale by scope), writes the audit record with cached true on a hit, and after a successful mutating run purges the server cache of every read action its invalidates names and asks staticCacheFor(registry).invalidate(paths) to regenerate in the background every prerendered entry whose page declares a loader that loaderInvalidatedBy matches, recording the paths on the audit record; static entries regenerate through the zero-JS renderer the build registers. page.fallback render stores a generated entry on a miss through the in-flight map; not-found answers 404 without rendering. client/act.ts onMutate snapshots and sets every matching loader query from action.optimistic, onError restores, onSettled invalidates; the region carries data-rex-optimistic while shown and the sidecar region entry optimistic: true."
env_pipeline        = "vite/env-module.ts (rex:env, typed in vite/rex-app.d.ts): client exports the VITE_ values validated and inlined through define from .env, .env.local and .env.<mode> read with Vite's loadEnv; server exports a lazily validated object over the runtime source that server/context.ts exposes as context.env (process.env on node, bun and deno; the bindings createEdgeHandler hands to setRuntimeEnv per request). The generated server entry validates env.server once and exits with REX451, installs SIGTERM and SIGINT handlers that await the static cache settled() and the adapter close() under REX_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS, and sets keep-alive timeouts safe behind proxies. vite/boundary.ts derives the REX441 secret names from the server schema keys; check/rules/boundaries.ts process-env reports a process.env read in an action, flow, data or app/server module of an app that declares env. rex dev loads the same files into the in-process server."
endpoint_pipeline   = "server/routes/http.ts installs one route per action with http: builds RexContext, evaluates policy, coerces the input from the query string (GET) through the form coercion of server/form.ts or from the body (POST), runs the same router procedure (audit, span), answers JSON or a string output under contentType; a POST keeps the Origin check unless csrf false is declared with a non-always policy; security/http-post-open reports a POST endpoint with policy always() or csrf false without a policy. vite/outputs/endpoints.ts writes every GET endpoint whose input accepts {} to dist/client<path>. server/routes/redirect.ts answers Location with the declared status before the render route; vite/outputs/redirects.ts writes the static stubs. server/routes/sitemap.ts answers /sitemap.xml (manifest pages without params allowed to the anonymous actor and not noindex, plus every prerendered path with lastmod and hreflang alternates) and /robots.txt (Disallow /rex/rpc, /rex/form, /rex/flow, the Sitemap line); vite/outputs/sitemap.ts, robots.ts and llms.ts write the same files plus llms.txt (app name, one line per prerendered path with title and index.md URL, one for rex/manifest) when site.origin is set, with one notice otherwise; document/second-sitemap reports a public/sitemap.xml or a robots.txt naming another sitemap while site.origin is set."
shell_derivation    = "client/shell/components.ts ShellComponents gains frames: Record<string, FrameComponent> and the Frame receives sectionLinks, trail and icons; vite/shell-components.ts validates the frames export (REX120); client/shell.tsx renders the named frame keyed by chrome.frame with data-rex-frame; useNavLinks sorts by chrome.order then id and carries icon; the trail follows chrome.back transitively (buildManifest rejects a cycle); the default Frame renders a secondary nav aria-label of the section and a breadcrumb nav of a[data-rex-nav] links; the palette groups Pages by frame in the same order; designx/index.ts maps the breadcrumbs surface to the trail slot; parity/frame-missing reports chrome.frame naming an export the ui.components module lacks."
i18n_pipeline       = "vite/prerender.ts expands every path once per locale under prefix routing (/<locale><path>), records locale on StaticPageEntry (prerender list version 2) and writes the locale chooser root document through vite/outputs/locale-chooser.ts; adapters/static-cache.ts keys entries by path and locale; server/middleware/locale.ts answers 307 to the resolved locale for an unprefixed document request, sets Content-Language and merges Accept-Language and Cookie into Vary; server/routes/locale.ts sets the rex-locale cookie by form post under routing none; client/shell/locale-slot.tsx renders one control per locale with data-rex-locale, lang and aria-pressed, as links under prefix routing and as a form under none; the palette lists the locale entries; client/i18n/defaults.ts holds the rex.* English defaults consulted after the app's files (rex.notFound.title, rex.back, rex.palette.placeholder, rex.confirm.*, rex.locale.switch); server/form.ts writes lang and the localized copy of the confirmation and error pages; i18n.direction sets dir on the document and in the sidecar; check/rules/i18n.ts gains missing-key, locale-parity and static-locale (several locales, routing none, a prerendered page) and reads placeholder, alt and aria-description attributes."
dev_loop_pipeline   = "vite/config-file.ts reads rex.config.ts from the resolved Vite root in configResolved and applies ui, shellComponents, fonts, i18n, compiler, devtools, tailwind, images, env and secretNames unless rex({ configFile: false }); boundaryHook runs only for builds and rex dev. vite/check.ts re-runs the synchronous rules on hotUpdate scoped to the changed page folder and sends findings as a rex:notice event; the devtools store gains recordFindings and recordError, the panels Check (data-rex-devtools-finding rows with rule, file:line, hint and link) and Errors (data-rex-devtools-error rows with code, message, hint, docs link, address and stack), the slot renders a visible button data-rex-devtools-toggle and opens a panel from ?devtools=<panel>; rex check --watch runs the same incremental checker from the terminal; in dev RegionErrorFallback adds a details block data-rex-dev-error removed by the REX_DEVTOOLS define. testing/playwright.ts exports readManifest, readSidecar, expectAddressed, expectParity, invokeByClick, invokeByShortcut, invokeByUrl, invokeByPalette, confirm, openOverlay, dismissByEscape, dismissByButton, setDensity, expectNoFailedRequests, walkPage and the gate runners walkNoJs, auditAxe, measureVitals, auditLighthouse (mobile and desktop) and checkScreenFit, parameterised by manifest and base URL and reading thresholds from rex.config budgets.lighthouse and budgets.vitals."
assets_pipeline     = "vite/images.ts (REX_HOOKS) transforms at build every Img src under public/ or an imported asset into dist/client/_rex/img/<hash>-<width>.<format> for each images.sizes width not above the intrinsic width and each images.formats format through sharp, publishes the map as the virtual module rex:images, and serves the variants on demand in dev; client/media.tsx Img reads the map, writes srcset when sizes is set and srcSet is not, renders a picture element with one source per extra format, throws REX314 for a remote src outside images.remote and keeps the priority preload with imagesrcset and imagesizes; media/img-sizes and media/remote-image-origin are the rules. vite/fonts.ts reads the OS/2 and hhea tables of a local font file (no dependency) into FontSpec.metrics for the fallback face and injects the preload links and style block into the client index.html through transformIndexHtml for the production client build and the dev shell; tokens/font-family reports a font-family literal in a part or region that is not the configured variable or a generic family."
hosts               = "cli/hosts/index.ts: HOST_TARGETS maps node, bun, deno, docker, deno-deploy, cloudflare, vercel, netlify, github-pages and static to one build target each (cloudflare to edge, vercel to node or edge by deploy.runtime, netlify to node, deno-deploy to deno, docker and node to node, bun to bun, github-pages and static to static); rex build without --target reads deploy.host; each writer receives the BuildResult and the manifest: cloudflare writes dist/wrangler.jsonc (main, compatibility_date, assets directory, binding, html_handling, not_found_handling, run_worker_first for /rex/* and every ssr and csr route); vercel writes dist/.vercel/output/config.json with routes and the cache headers table, static/ from dist/client, functions/rex.func with .vc-config.json and a prerender-config per revalidate page; netlify writes dist/netlify.toml and dist/.netlify/v1/functions/rex.mjs with preferStatic; deno-deploy writes dist/deno.json with tasks.start; docker writes dist/Dockerfile (node, bun or deno image, HOST 0.0.0.0, USER, EXPOSE, HEALTHCHECK on /rex/health) and dist/.dockerignore; github-pages writes dist/client/.nojekyll and refuses a page with route params that is neither ssg nor static; every writer emits the declared redirects natively and prints one wrote line and a start hint; the manifest carries deploy { host, target }; check/rules/deploy.ts host-target reports revalidate on a host whose target has no page store, a page with params on github-pages that is not prerendered, and a mutating action on a static host without client.apiOrigin, and deploy/config a deploy.host that is not a literal. cli/commands/preview.ts serves dist/server.js through the node adapter or dist/client through adapters/static-host.ts (index resolution, 404.html, content types, Accept-CH, the _headers table) and prints rex preview: serving <url>."
generators          = "cli/commands/make.ts: rex make page <id> [--route] [--render] [--load <action,...>] (a params route with ssg or static writes an empty paths for the author), rex make page not-found, rex make action <name> --read [--route <path>], rex make loader <page> <name> --action <action> (adds the load entry and hooks/use<Name>.ts), rex make collection <name> (entity, app/content/<name>/, app/data/<name>.ts, list and read actions, list and detail pages with paths { action, map }), rex make test <page>; cli/gen/test.ts writes vitest.config.ts as defineConfig({ plugins: rex(), test: rexVitest() }) with the test dependencies at the pinned versions and the page test template that renders the page for the anonymous actor and asserts data-rex-page, every region and every action in readSidecar(); cli/gen/repo.ts writes .gitignore, README.md and .env.example from the env schema and runs git init with an initial commit unless --no-git; cli/commands/upgrade.ts rewrites the pinned dependencies through cli/versions.ts, installs, runs the codemods for the detected version and ends with rex check; cli/commands/add.ts installs DesignX registry items through addDesignx; check/rules/tests.ts page-has-test warns on a page folder without a test; cli/gen/site.ts and gen/example.ts implement the templates decision."
demo_usage          = "examples/demo adopts every feature in the last wave: site, deploy.host, env, redirects, prefetch and images.remote in rex.config; chrome.description, order and icon on every page; a docs frame shared by about and tokens; a collection app/content/notes rendered by Prose on about through a read action and a static page with paths { action, map }; islands on about (the copy region visible) and tokens (the filter idle); a not-found page folder; rest route /docs/:path* on a new reference page; action.http on list-tokens (GET /tokens.json) and a sitemap, robots and llms from the manifest; action.cache on load-wallet; optimistic on toggle-hide-dust; a Link in the portfolio hero; a locale switcher and translated portfolio and send with the allow list shrunk to brand names; an Img with sizes; the walk, vitals, Lighthouse (performance, accessibility, best practices and SEO) and no-JS gates through the shipped helpers with the SEO thresholds of the site."
site_template       = "rex new <name> --template site writes rex.config.ts (render default static, site { origin }, deploy { host: github-pages }, ui designx with app/components/Shell.tsx), package.json scripts (dev, build, build:static, preview, check, manifest, test, test:unit, test:e2e, lint, format), index.html without a title, app/content/docs with one markdown page, app/entities/doc.ts, app/data/docs.ts (contentStore), app/actions/list-docs.ts and read-doc.ts, pages home (ssg: Hero and Index regions), doc (/docs/:slug, static, paths { action, map }, Article with Prose and Toc regions), not-found, a docs frame, public/ with robots.txt absent (derived) and the mark, e2e/operability.spec.ts over walkPage and playwright.config.ts with phone, tablet and desktop projects, vitest.config.ts and a page test per page."
testing             = "Every task's verify_cmd is vitest files under packages/rex, rex check or rex build on examples/demo, or both, under 15 minutes; browser suites run once per wave on the merged revision. Fixture apps live beside the tests (packages/rex/src/check/fixtures/<rule>, src/cli/fixtures, src/vite/fixtures, src/testing/fixtures) and never under a task's touches unless named. New rules get a fixture folder and a test naming each finding."

[documentation]
mode      = "auto"
status    = "pending"
audiences = ["user", "developer", "agent"]
targets   = ["README.md", "docs/primitives.md", "docs/convention.md", "docs/agent-contract.md", "docs/architecture.md", "docs/platforms.md", "docs/cli.md", "docs/errors.md", "docs/tutorial.md", "docs/recipes/README.md", "docs/recipes/document-head.md", "docs/recipes/navigation.md", "docs/recipes/content-collection.md", "docs/recipes/islands.md", "docs/recipes/deploy.md", "docs/recipes/env.md", "docs/recipes/endpoints.md", "docs/recipes/server-middleware.md", "docs/recipes/static-page.md", "docs/recipes/loader.md", "docs/recipes/i18n.md", "docs/recipes/designx.md"]

[req.1]
title = "The declarations grow, the contract follows"
story = "As an agent writing a Rex app, I want every 0.3 capability to be a field on a declaration I already know so that the manifest, the sidecar and rex check tell me about it without a new file convention."
ac_1  = "page() accepts chrome.description, image, frame, order and icon, islands, prefetch, fallback, a rest route segment and paths { action, map }; action() accepts http, cache and optimistic; defineConfig accepts site, redirects, deploy, env, prefetch, security.forwarded, images.remote, fonts[].variable and fallback and i18n.direction; each invalid value throws its REX code with the field name and the tests in core name every code."
ac_2  = "buildManifest writes every new field, validates action.invalidates names, http path collisions and redirect sources, and AGENTS.md lists redirects, deploy, endpoints, islands and locales; the sidecar payload carries document, loaders, locale, locales, direction, frame and the region island and optimistic fields and validates against sidecar.schema.ts; the text renderer prints the Loaders table."
ac_3  = "@sidioralabs/rex/errors exports the catalog with hints and areas and resolves in the packed tarball with types; the demo and the site pass rex check unchanged."

[req.2]
title = "A declared document head"
story = "As a site author, I want every page to carry its title per path, description, canonical and social tags so that Rex sites pass Lighthouse SEO like an Astro site does."
ac_1  = "A server-rendered and a prerendered document carry one title through site.titleTemplate with {param} placeholders filled, a meta description, a canonical link from site.origin, og and twitter tags, hreflang alternates under prefix routing and a rel=alternate link to the markdown rendering; the h1, the announcer, the text renderer and the sidecar document field carry the same resolved title and description."
ac_2  = "The non-script head of the app's index.html reaches dev and production documents with the Rex-owned tags filtered; the form confirmation and error pages use the same head; a static page ships no module script, modulepreload or rex+data script from the dev server, the node build and the edge target, and a missing ActionForm is REX405 at render in dev."
ac_3  = "After a client navigation document.title, the canonical link and the description equal the sidecar document; check/rules/document.ts reports shared-title, no-description, index-html-owned-tag, image-missing and site-origin with file and line, and parity/runtime compares the rendered title with the sidecar."

[req.3]
title = "One way to navigate, on every page, with or without JavaScript"
story = "As an agent operating a Rex app, I want every link to be an addressed anchor that works before hydration so that a static page and a hydrated page offer the same controls."
ac_1  = "Link renders a[data-rex-nav] with the typed href from the page declaration or a page id of the generated RexPageId union, navigates through the route change with the target's transition, validates params in dev and navigates by document under REX_STATIC_HOST; parity/nav-target reports a page id string that names no page folder."
ac_2  = "The back and recovery controls are Links with the target href, so they resolve on a prerendered static page with JavaScript disabled; a push scrolls to the top or the URL hash after the transition and a traverse restores the previous position; nav.to and Link accept scroll false."
ac_3  = "A throw in view.tsx, states.tsx or a region outside a RegionBoundary renders the page's RecoverableError under main[data-rex-page-error] with REX335 in the outcome store and the reserved region id page in the sidecar regions, with a retry that remounts; a throw in the shell renders the startup error markup with Retry."

[req.4]
title = "Prerendered pages on every target with CDN caching"
story = "As an operator, I want prerendered pages cached by the CDN and served on the edge target so that a Rex deployment performs like an Astro or Next.js one behind a proxy."
ac_1  = "A prerendered page for the anonymous actor answers public, s-maxage and must-revalidate or stale-while-revalidate derived from revalidate, Vary carries Cookie, x-rex-density and the Client Hint names, an actor or ssr render answers private, no-store, index.md follows its page, GET /rex/manifest answers an ETag and 304, hashed assets are immutable on the node adapter and dist/client/_headers carries the same table on the static target."
ac_2  = "rex build --target edge writes the prerendered pages, index.md and dist/prerender.json, the edge entry serves them through installEdgeStaticPages with the Cache API store and regenerates a stale revalidate page after the response through waitUntil, answering the same x-rex-static status as node."
ac_3  = "With security.forwarded true a POST to /rex/rpc through a proxy that sets X-Forwarded-Host and X-Forwarded-Proto passes the Origin check and CORS; without it the check compares the request URL as today."

[req.5]
title = "Content as data"
story = "As a site author, I want markdown files to be typed entries listed and read like any Rex data so that a Rex site has what Astro collections give and the agent reads the markdown source."
ac_1  = "memoryStore, drizzleStore and contentStore pass the conformance suite for sort, range and in queries; a markdown() field renders to html with heading ids, a headings list and highlighted code through renderMarkdown; Prose renders the html under data-rex-prose through unsafeHtml and Toc renders the headings as links."
ac_2  = "contentStore lists and gets entries from app/content/<name> validated by the entity, with the key from the file slug and the body in the markdown field; paths { action, map } runs the read action through the router with policy, validation and audit at prerender; content/invalid-entry, content/unbound and parity/paths-handler report with file and line; the content role is importable by no role."
ac_3  = "rex make collection <name> writes an entity, a content folder, a data module, two read actions and two pages that pass rex check; the text renderer of a page whose loader returns a markdown field appends the markdown source after the sidecar."

[req.6]
title = "Deploy anywhere with one switch, preview everywhere"
story = "As an operator, I want rex build to write the files my host needs and rex preview to serve the result so that deploying a Rex app is one config field."
ac_1  = "deploy.host selects the build target and the writer: cloudflare writes wrangler.jsonc, vercel .vercel/output with config.json, static/, the function and prerender-config files, netlify netlify.toml and the function, deno-deploy deno.json, docker Dockerfile and .dockerignore, github-pages .nojekyll; each writes the declared redirects natively; the manifest records deploy { host, target } and the start hint names the host's command."
ac_2  = "dist/ copied alone to a directory without node_modules starts with node server.js and answers /rex/health 200 and the rex: serving line; deploy/host-target reports revalidate on a host without a page store, a params page on github-pages that is not prerendered, and a mutating action on a static host without client.apiOrigin."
ac_3  = "rex preview serves a node build through the node adapter and a static build through adapters/static-host.ts with index resolution, 404.html, content types, Accept-CH and the _headers table, printing rex preview: serving <url>; the site's Playwright webServer and tools/smoke-package.sh use it."

[req.7]
title = "The region is the island"
story = "As a site author, I want a static page to hydrate only the region that needs JavaScript so that a Rex site ships as little JavaScript as an Astro site."
ac_1  = "A static page with islands ships only the listed regions' chunks and one boot script, each region hydrating at load, idle or visible with data-rex-island and data-rex-hydrated, adopting the page's sidecar script and handling ?act= on boot; the chunk table lists island chunks under the page budget."
ac_2  = "On an ssr or ssg page a region declared idle or visible keeps its server HTML visible until its chunk arrives and a never region stays server-only with its actions as forms; the manifest lists pages[].islands and the sidecar region entries carry island."
ac_3  = "render/static-needs-js reports a non-island region of a static page importing act, useAct, useOverlay, useLoader, useStore or a page hook with the hint to declare it in islands or render an ActionForm; render/region-needs-js reports a never region referencing an action with a shortcut; parity/runtime mounts islands and checks their controls against the sidecar."

[req.8]
title = "Static sites in every locale"
story = "As a reader of a multilingual Rex site, I want every page in my locale at its own address so that a static host serves it with no redirect JavaScript."
ac_1  = "Under prefix routing rex build writes one index.html, index.md and sidecar per locale and path, the root document is a locale chooser with addressed links and a meta refresh, the static cache keys by path and locale, and i18n/static-locale reports several locales with routing none on a prerendered page."
ac_2  = "The server answers 307 to the resolved locale for an unprefixed document request and sets Content-Language and Vary; the sidecar, manifest and AGENTS.md carry locale, locales and direction; the shell locale switcher renders one control per locale with data-rex-locale as links under prefix routing and as a form under none, the palette lists them and ?locale= switches."
ac_3  = "Framework chrome strings resolve through rex.* messages with shipped English defaults and the confirmation and error pages carry lang and the localized copy; i18n/missing-key reports an undefined key and i18n/locale-parity a key or ICU argument that differs between locale files; placeholder, alt and aria-description are checked like label."

[req.9]
title = "Findings in the browser, the walk in the package"
story = "As a developer, I want rex check findings and runtime errors in the devtools while I edit and the operability walk shipped as a library so that every Rex app proves the agent contract the way the demo does."
ac_1  = "rex() called from vitest.config.ts picks up ui.components, fonts, i18n, images, env and secretNames from rex.config.ts and ships no rex:boundary plugin under test; the demo and site vitest configs are plugins: rex()."
ac_2  = "Editing a region to import another page sends a boundaries/cross-page finding to the devtools Check panel with rule, file:line, hint and docs link within one hot update and prints the same line in rex dev; rex check --watch re-reports on change; a REX307 thrown from a region lists in the Errors panel and renders the dev details block; the devtools open by click on data-rex-devtools-toggle, by shortcut and by ?devtools=sidecar."
ac_3  = "@sidioralabs/rex/testing/playwright exports the walk helpers and gate runners; the demo and site walks import them and the helper test runs walkPage against the fixture app served by rex preview."

[req.10]
title = "Images and fonts from the declaration"
story = "As a site author, I want images resized and converted at build and fonts served without layout shift so that Rex pages hit the vitals an Astro or Next.js page hits."
ac_1  = "rex build writes the images.sizes by images.formats variants of a local Img source, Img with sizes renders srcset from them and a picture element with one source per extra format, the priority preload carries imagesrcset and imagesizes, a remote src outside images.remote throws REX314 and media/img-sizes and media/remote-image-origin report with file and line."
ac_2  = "A FontSpec with a local src emits :root { --font-<name> } and a Family Fallback face with size-adjust, ascent-override, descent-override and line-gap-override computed from the file, in SSR, prerendered pages, csr documents and the static shells; tokens/font-family reports a font-family literal that is not the variable or a generic family."

[req.11]
title = "The routing contract: every path answers correctly"
story = "As an agent, I want an unknown path, a nested content path, an old URL and a missing record to answer the status and page the manifest predicts."
ac_1  = "A route ending in :path* matches any depth, params.path is a string array on client, server, prerender and the text renderer, pageHref and nav.href join it, the manifest marks the param rest and the JSON schema says array of strings."
ac_2  = "An app with app/pages/not-found renders it for an unmatched path with data-rex-page not-found, the sidecar and the outcome region, the server answers 404 with its HTML and markdown, the static target writes it as 404.html with zero JavaScript, the palette and nav exclude it; an app without it keeps the built-in fallback."
ac_3  = "Invalid route params and a loader NOT_FOUND answer 404 with the TerminalError state, a loader FORBIDDEN answers 403, other failures stay 500, x-rex-render names the kind and the text route answers the same statuses; an unmatched path that a declared redirect covers resolves on the client to the destination with replace."

[req.12]
title = "Mutations drive every cache"
story = "As an app author, I want a mutating action's invalidates to refresh the client, the server cache and the prerendered pages, and the region to show the optimistic value meanwhile."
ac_1  = "A read action with cache { maxAge } answers from the server cache within maxAge for the same input and actor or locale by scope, every call still writes an audit record with cached true, the policy runs before the cache, and a mutating action whose invalidates names it purges the entry."
ac_2  = "After a mutating action succeeds every prerendered entry whose page loader it invalidates regenerates in the background and the audit record lists the paths; a static page regenerates through the zero-JS renderer; page.fallback render stores a generated entry on the first miss and not-found answers 404; render/regenerate-unreachable warns where the target cannot regenerate."
ac_3  = "While a mutation with optimistic is pending the matching loader queries show next(current, input), the region carries data-rex-optimistic and the sidecar region entry optimistic true, both cleared on settle; an error restores the snapshot; parity/runtime asserts the attribute clears."

[req.13]
title = "A typed env and a server entry that shuts down cleanly"
story = "As an operator, I want secrets validated at start, never bundled, and reachable in handlers on every runtime so that the same action runs on node and on the edge."
ac_1  = "rex:env exports client with the VITE_ values validated and inlined and server with the schema-validated values from process.env or the edge bindings; a client import of server is REX440; the built server exits with REX451 naming a missing or invalid key; handlers read ctx.env and app/server modules import { env } from rex:env; boundaries/process-env reports process.env in an action, flow, data or app/server module."
ac_2  = "rex dev loads .env, .env.local and .env.<mode> into the in-process server; the generated entry stops on SIGTERM and SIGINT after the static cache settled and the adapter closed within REX_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS and exits at once on a second signal; the node adapter keeps alive 65 seconds behind proxies."

[req.14]
title = "Derived endpoints and derived files"
story = "As a site author, I want a sitemap, a robots file, an llms.txt, a feed and a JSON endpoint without writing a route so that crawlers and agents read the same inventory the manifest lists."
ac_1  = "An action with http answers GET or POST at its path through the router with policy, validation and audit, as JSON or a string body under contentType, the manifest and AGENTS.md list it, a GET endpoint whose input accepts {} is written to dist/client<path> on every target that prerenders, and security/http-post-open reports an open POST endpoint."
ac_2  = "With site.origin set the server answers /sitemap.xml and /robots.txt and the static target writes sitemap.xml, robots.txt and llms.txt from the manifest and the prerender list with hreflang alternates and lastmod; a declared redirect answers Location with its status before the render route and the static target writes its meta-refresh stub with a canonical link and a data-rex-nav link; site/scripts/sitemap.mjs and site/public/robots.txt are deleted and tools/site-verify.mjs reads the derived files."

[req.15]
title = "The shell is derived, sections included"
story = "As an app author, I want section navigation, nav order, icons, breadcrumbs and prefetch from the page declarations so that no Shell override hand-codes a navigation table."
ac_1  = "Pages sharing chrome.frame render inside the named frame export with data-rex-frame, the frame persists across navigations inside the section and receives the section links and the breadcrumb trail from chrome.back, each link a[data-rex-nav]; the default Frame renders both navs; parity/frame-missing reports a frame the ui.components module lacks."
ac_2  = "The derived navigation and the palette Pages group sort by chrome.order then id and carry chrome.icon; a page's chunk and declared loaders prefetch on pointerenter and focus (hover) or viewport entry per page.prefetch or the config default, never under saveData, 2g or agent density, and a static build prefetches the target document instead."

[req.16]
title = "Generators and hygiene from the first command"
story = "As a developer starting a Rex app, I want the generated project to carry its tests, ignores, env example and upgrade path so that the first commit is clean and the next version is one command."
ac_1  = "rex make page accepts --route, --render and --load and writes a params route with paths for a prerendered page, rex make page not-found writes the reserved page, rex make action --read and rex make loader write the one loader pattern, rex make test writes the page test; every generated page passes rex check."
ac_2  = "rex new writes vitest.config.ts with rexVitest(), the test dependencies, a page test per page, .gitignore, README.md and .env.example and runs git init with an initial commit unless --no-git; rex upgrade rewrites the pinned dependencies, installs, runs the codemods for the detected version and ends with rex check; rex add installs DesignX items; tests/page-has-test warns on a page folder without a test."

[req.17]
title = "The demo and the site template use every feature"
story = "As a reader of the docs, I want the demo and rex new --template site to show every adopted feature working so that nothing in 0.3 is a claim without a running example."
ac_1  = "examples/demo uses every feature of [design] demo_usage, rex check reports zero findings, the unit tests pass, rex build on node, edge and static writes the derived files, and the walk, no-JS, axe, vitals and Lighthouse gates pass through the shipped helpers with the SEO threshold."
ac_2  = "rex new <name> --template site writes [design] site_template, rex check exits 0, rex build --target static writes every page, 404.html, sitemap.xml, robots.txt, llms.txt and index.md per page, and the generated operability spec walks it; rex new --example demo installs the example and --host fills deploy.host and the start script."

[task.0.1]
title = "Declaration groundwork: the 0.3 page, action, config and context fields, their REX codes, the manifest, AGENTS.md, the sidecar and the errors entry"
status = "done"
mode = "BUILD"
wave = 0
requires = []
reqs = ["1.1", "1.2", "1.3"]
do_1 = "Implement [design] declaration_surface and [design] errors in core: parseRoute with the rest segment, PageChrome with description, image, frame, order and icon and resolveChromeText for {param} placeholders, page islands, prefetch, fallback, paths as a function or { action, map } and the reserved id not-found; action http, cache and optimistic with ActionContext { actor, env, locale, density }; defineConfig site, redirects, deploy, env (two schemas written with the rex/schema helpers, client keys VITE_), prefetch, security.forwarded, images.remote, fonts[].variable and fallback, i18n.direction; RESERVED_QUERY_KEYS gains locale and devtools; the catalog gains REX124 to REX127, REX225 to REX230, REX335 and REX451 with hints and areas; server/router.ts fills env, locale and density on the handler context from RexContext and runFlow with null and the default density; vite/prerender.ts expandPagePaths runs { action, map } through the ledger-backed loader runner as the anonymous actor."
