do_1 = "Implement [design] head_pipeline in server/ssr.ts: documentHead takes the page, the validated params, site, locale and the settled loader client and emits the resolved title through site.titleTemplate, meta description, canonical, og and twitter tags, robots, hreflang alternates plus x-default under prefix routing, the rel=alternate text/markdown link, the font-face block with the family variable and the fallback face when FontSpec carries metrics, then assets.head filtered of owned tags; the renderer renders a static page with hydrate false and emits no module script, modulepreload or rex+data script in every environment, running the missing-forms check as REX405 at render in dev; the resolved document is passed to the sidecar document field and the announcer; server/form.ts builds the confirmation and error pages through the same head helper; routes/pages-text.ts prints the resolved title, description and canonical; vite/ssr-css.ts readSsrAssets reads the non-script head of dist/client/index.html and vite/ssr.ts transforms the app's own index.html in dev through a shared headOf helper."
do_2 = "client/shell/document.tsx, registered in client/shell/slots.ts, renders nothing and on route change sets document.title and replaces the canonical link and the description meta from the sidecar document field; check/rules/document.ts, registered in check/rules/index.ts, reports document/shared-title (a params route rendered ssg or static whose title has no placeholder), document/no-description (a prerendered page with neither chrome.description nor site.description), document/index-html-owned-tag, document/image-missing (chrome.image or site.image naming a public/ file that does not exist) and document/site-origin (canonical, alternates or a sitemap requested without site.origin); check/rules/i18n.ts treats chrome.description like title; check/runtime.ts asserts per page and actor exactly one title equal to the sidecar document, a description, one canonical and html lang."
