do_1 = "Implement [design] islands_runtime: vite/split.ts adds the island-<page>-<region> chunk group measured under the page budget and printed in the chunk table; vite/app-module.ts imports a region listed in page.islands through its own loader; server/ssr.ts emits for a static page one modulepreload per island and one nonce'd boot script after the sidecar, and for a hydrated page wraps an idle or visible region in a Suspense boundary whose lazy importer resolves at the declared moment so React's selective hydration keeps the server HTML; a never region renders server-only; vite/ssr-css.ts lists island assets; client/islands.ts hydrates a section with hydrateRoot through the provider stack of client/interop/mount.tsx scoped to the page runtime, now for load, on requestIdleCallback for idle, on IntersectionObserver for visible, adopts the page's existing sidecar script (RexSidecar accepts the adopted script) and handles ?act= on boot; client/page.tsx sets data-rex-island and data-rex-hydrated on the section and client/lazy.ts gains the deferred importer."
do_2 = "check/rules/render.ts extends static-needs-js (a non-island region of a static page importing act, useAct, useOverlay, useLoader, useStore or a page hook, with the hint to declare it in islands or render an ActionForm) and adds region-needs-js (a never region referencing an action with a shortcut or opening a region-bound overlay); check/runtime.ts mounts islands and checks their controls against the sidecar; the sidecar region entries carry island."
do_3 = "Tests: split.test.ts, app-module.test.ts, ssr-css.test.ts, ssr.test.tsx (the static document with island preloads and the boot script, the hydrated document with the boundary), islands.test.tsx with injected requestIdleCallback and IntersectionObserver of the real shapes, page.test.tsx, lazy.test.tsx, sidecar.test.tsx, render.test.ts with fixtures under check/fixtures/render, runtime.test.ts; the demo builds with --target static; docs/recipes/islands.md is the recipe linked from docs/recipes/README.md; docs/convention.md and docs/agent-contract.md document islands and the two attributes."
