do_1 = "Rest segments: client/router.tsx parsePageParams splits the matched remainder on / and decodes each segment, pageHref joins an encoded array, the wouter route becomes a wildcard mapped back to the param name, server/ssr.ts matchPage compiles the rest pattern, routes/pages-text.ts pathRouteParams and vite/prerender.ts routePath handle arrays and nest directories; the not-found page: RexRoutes resolves an unmatched path first against the declared redirects (a replace navigation to the destination with the params carried over) and then to a PageResolution of the not-found page with params { path }, the body slot renders it through PageHost with data-rex-page not-found, the sidecar and the header title, and client/fallbacks.tsx keeps the built-in section (titled by msg:rex.notFound.title) for apps without it."
do_2 = "Statuses: render() in server/ssr.ts maps resolution issues to kind not-found (404) while rendering the matched page's TerminalError state, a loader RexLoaderError status 404 to not-found, 403 to denied, other terminal 4xx to not-found with TerminalError, everything else to failed (500) with RecoverableError, and an unmatched path with a not-found page to that page's HTML with 404; routes/render.ts maps the kinds in RENDER_STATUS and x-rex-render; pages-text.ts answers the same statuses and the not-found page's markdown; vite/outputs/not-found.ts prerenders the not-found page (zero-JS) into 404.html in place of the shell document when the app declares one; testing/index.ts renderPage accepts the not-found page and an unmatched path."
